                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Fig. 2.14: Structure of a mitochondrion"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.442,
            0.267,
            0.888,
            0.306
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Mitochondria — The powerhouse of the cell"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.442,
            0.309,
            0.89,
            0.362
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Mitochondria are often called the ‘powerhouses of the cell’ because they supply the energy needed for most cellular activities. Each mitochondrion (Fig."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.444,
            0.361,
            0.805,
            0.379
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "2.14) is surrounded by two membranes :"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.45,
            0.381,
            0.804,
            0.416
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "y The "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "outer membrane",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " is smooth and porous."
            }
          ]
        },
